NNAAMMEE
     hhccsseeccdd — control link keys and PIN codes for Bluetooth devices

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     hhccsseeccdd [--ddhh] --ff _c_o_n_f_i_g_f_i_l_e

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The hhccsseeccdd daemon controls link keys and PIN codes for Bluetooth devices.
     It opens a raw HCI socket and listens for Link_Key_Request,
     PIN_Code_Request and Link_Key_Notification HCI events.

     Once a Link_Key_Request or PIN_Code_Request HCI event is received, the
     daemon scans the configuration file for a matching entry.  The remote de‐
     vice BD_ADDR is used as a key.  If no matching entry was found, the de‐
     fault entry will be used.  If no default entry was found then it is as‐
     sumed that no link key and no PIN code exists.  For any given entry, the
     link key takes precedence over the PIN code.  If a link key was not spec‐
     ified, the device must generate the link key from the PIN code.  If an
     entry was found and the link key (or PIN code) exists, the
     Link_Key_Request_Reply (or PIN_Code_Request_Reply) command will be sent
     back to the device.  Otherwise, the Link_Key_Request_Negative_Reply (or
     PIN_Code_Request_Negative_Reply) command will be sent back to the device.

     The hhccsseeccdd daemon also handles HCI Link_Key_Notification events and
     caches link keys created from the PIN codes in memory.  To preserve link
     keys between restarts the hhccsseeccdd daemon dumps link keys for all entries
     in the _/_v_a_r_/_d_b_/_h_c_s_e_c_d_._k_e_y_s link keys file.  If it exists, the link keys
     file gets processed by the hhccsseeccdd daemon after it processes its main con‐
     figuration file.  The link keys file gets written every time the hhccsseeccdd
     daemon shuts down gracefully.  It is possible to force the hhccsseeccdd daemon
     to re-read its main configuration file and dump the link keys file by
     sending the HUP signal to the hhccsseeccdd process.  The user is expected to
     not modify the link keys file by hand.

     The command line options are as follows:

     --dd      Do not detach from the controlling terminal.

     --ff _c_o_n_f_i_g_f_i_l_e
             Specify the name of the configuration file.  The default is
             _/_e_t_c_/_b_l_u_e_t_o_o_t_h_/_h_c_s_e_c_d_._c_o_n_f.

     --hh      Display usage message and exit.

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/bluetooth/hcsecd.conf
     /var/db/hcsecd.keys
     /var/run/hcsecd.pid

